# BINARY output and CENTER's report (cmdref: Plot types; Beam set-up), on the manual's CassWithExitPupil.in.
# BINARY: BINOUT opened the direct-access file with RECL=(4*NC), a SUN-era word count for a REAL*8 row -- gfortran
#   (bytes) died with 'Write exceeds length of DIRECT access record', ifx (words) padded every record to twice its
#   length (1048576 bytes for 256 x 256).  Now INQUIRE(IOLENGTH=) sizes the record: 256*256*8 = 524288 bytes on both
#   compilers.  CENTER printed 'Beam centered in 0 iterations' (a literal 0); the aiming solve's count now reaches it.
#   Three debug prints are gone: '** In DBINOUT' (any TEXT plot), '*** CPERTURB src' (PERTURB of the source),
#   'Debug: VALUE' (MOD of Flux=).  macos-fd's TRANSCRIPT_DIFF 3.2 / 3.5 / 3.6; Dave 2026-10-19: fix, remove, pass.
# COPY: $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/CassWithExitPupil.in
cd $TMP
old CassWithExitPupil.in
int 6
/null
binary
int 6
/null
! wc -c < CassWithExitPupil.in.int6
text
opd 6
/null
center
5
0.01,0
perturb
0
1e-6,0,0
0,0,0
mod
Flux=0.01
q
# EXPECT: DIRECT ACCESS File=CassWithExitPupil\.in\.int6
# EXPECT: ^\s*524288\s*$
# EXPECT: Beam centered in\s+[1-9]\d* iterations
# EXPECT: Flux\s+=\s+1\.0+(E|D)-02
# EXPECT-NOT: In DBINOUT
# EXPECT-NOT: CPERTURB src
# EXPECT-NOT: Debug: VALUE
# EXPECT-NOT: Write exceeds
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
